@flexiarg operator/praise-the-worker-then-bring-in-a-strategist
@title Praise The Worker, Then Bring In A Strategist For The Block
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-65fI2n turn-vNzuFa; first proposed for: One agent is doing well on the work and has hit a block of defects all at once.
@why [orchestration/recorded-handoff]

! conclusion: Read the pointed lines, advise on direction, and leave the work with the worker.

  + IF:
    The operator praises it, then asks another agent to look at the issues and give strategic advice, pointing to the lines in its buffer.

  + HOWEVER:
    The strategist has no context; the worker may read it as a vote of no confidence.

  + THEN:
    Read the pointed lines, advise on direction, and leave the work with the worker.

  + BECAUSE:
    Strategy and execution are separate and the block is the point where strategy matters.
